      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-6 text-sm">
        
        <!-- PDF & CDF Rules -->
        <div class="p-4 border border-slate-200 rounded-xl bg-slate-50 space-y-2">
          <h4 class="font-bold text-slate-800 flex items-center gap-2">
            <span>⚖️</span> PDF & CDF Axioms
          </h4>
          <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-1 text-slate-700 text-xs leading-relaxed">
            <li><strong>Non-negativity:</strong> $f_X(x) \ge 0$ for all $x$.</li>
            <li><strong>Normalization:</strong> $\int_{-\infty}^\infty f_X(x) dx = 1$.</li>
            <li><strong>Single point probability:</strong> $P(X = c) = 0$. Hence $P(a \le X \le b) = P(a < X < b)$.</li>
            <li><strong>Fundamental link:</strong> $F_X(x) = \int_{-\infty}^x f(t)dt \implies f_X(x) = F'_X(x)$.</li>
            <li><strong>Median $m$:</strong> Satisfies $F_X(m) = 0.5$ or $\int_{-\infty}^m f(x)dx = 0.5$.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <!-- Moments & Linearity -->
        <div class="p-4 border border-slate-200 rounded-xl bg-slate-50 space-y-2">
          <h4 class="font-bold text-slate-800 flex items-center gap-2">
            <span>📈</span> Moments & Transformations
          </h4>
          <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-1 text-slate-700 text-xs leading-relaxed">
            <li><strong>Expectation:</strong> $E[X] = \int_{-\infty}^\infty x f(x) dx$ (requires $\int |x|f(x)dx < \infty$).</li>
            <li><strong>Non-negative shortcut:</strong> For $X \ge 0$, $E[X] = \int_0^\infty [1 - F_X(x)] dx$.</li>
            <li><strong>Variance Formula:</strong> $\text{Var}(X) = E[X^2] - (E[X])^2$.</li>
            <li><strong>Linearity of Expectation:</strong> $E[aX + b] = aE[X] + b$.</li>
            <li><strong>Linearity of Variance:</strong> $\text{Var}(aX + b) = a^2 \text{Var}(X)$.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <!-- Essential Integration -->
        <div class="p-4 border border-slate-200 rounded-xl bg-slate-50 space-y-2">
          <h4 class="font-bold text-slate-800 flex items-center gap-2">
            <span>📐</span> Calculus & Integration Techniques
          </h4>
          <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-1 text-slate-700 text-xs leading-relaxed">
            <li><strong>Integration by Parts:</strong> $\int u dv = uv - \int v du$.</li>
            <li><strong>Standard Form:</strong> $\int x e^{-kx} dx = -\frac{x}{k}e^{-kx} - \frac{1}{k^2}e^{-kx} + C$.</li>
            <li><strong>Power tails:</strong> $\int_1^\infty \frac{1}{x^p} dx$ converges if and only if $p > 1$.</li>
            <li><strong>Symmetry:</strong> If $f(x)$ is symmetric about $\alpha$, then $E[X] = \text{median} = \alpha$ (if the mean exists).</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

