      <!-- Question 1 -->
      <div class="border border-slate-200 rounded-xl overflow-hidden">
        <div class="bg-slate-100 p-4 border-b border-slate-200">
          <div class="flex justify-between items-center">
            <span class="font-bold text-blue-700">Question 1 [50 Points]</span>
            <span class="text-xs bg-white text-slate-700 px-2.5 py-1 rounded-md border font-medium">Law of Total Probability & Exp Mixtures</span>
          </div>
          <p class="text-sm mt-2 text-slate-800">
            Let $Y \sim \text{Bernoulli}(0.5)$. The conditional distribution of $X$ given $Y$ is:
            <br />$X \mid Y=1 \sim \text{Exp}(4)$ and $X \mid Y=0 \sim \text{Exp}(2)$.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="p-4 space-y-4">
          <!-- (a) -->
          <div>
            <h5 class="text-sm font-bold text-slate-800">(a) Write down the two conditional probabilities $P(X \le x \mid Y=1)$ and $P(X \le x \mid Y=0)$.</h5>
            <button onclick="toggleSol('sol-1a')" class="mt-2 text-xs text-blue-600 hover:underline font-semibold">▶ Toggle Solution</button>
            <div id="sol-1a" class="hidden mt-2 p-3 bg-blue-50/60 rounded-lg text-sm space-y-1 border border-blue-100">
              <p>For an exponential variable $W \sim \text{Exp}(\lambda)$, the CDF is $F(x) = 1 - e^{-\lambda x}$ for $x \ge 0$, and $0$ for $x < 0$.</p>
              <p>For $x \ge 0$:</p>
              <p>$$P(X \le x \mid Y=1) = 1 - e^{-4x}$$</p>
              <p>$$P(X \le x \mid Y=0) = 1 - e^{-2x}$$</p>
              <p>(Both are $0$ when $x < 0$).</p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <!-- (b) -->
          <div class="border-t pt-3">
            <h5 class="text-sm font-bold text-slate-800">(b) Use the Law of Total Probability to find $F_X(x) = P(X \le x)$ separately for $x < 0$ and $x \ge 0$.</h5>
            <button onclick="toggleSol('sol-1b')" class="mt-2 text-xs text-blue-600 hover:underline font-semibold">▶ Toggle Solution</button>
            <div id="sol-1b" class="hidden mt-2 p-3 bg-blue-50/60 rounded-lg text-sm space-y-1 border border-blue-100">
              <p>By the Law of Total Probability:</p>
              <p>$$F_X(x) = P(X \le x \mid Y=1)P(Y=1) + P(X \le x \mid Y=0)P(Y=0)$$</p>
              <p>Given $P(Y=1) = 0.5$ and $P(Y=0) = 0.5$:</p>
              <ul class="list-disc list-inside mt-1 space-y-1">
                <li>For $x < 0$: $F_X(x) = 0(0.5) + 0(0.5) = 0$.</li>
                <li>For $x \ge 0$:
                  $$F_X(x) = 0.5(1 - e^{-4x}) + 0.5(1 - e^{-2x}) = 1 - \frac{1}{2}e^{-4x} - \frac{1}{2}e^{-2x}$$
                </li>
              </ul>
            </div>
          </div>

          <!-- (c) -->
          <div class="border-t pt-3">
            <h5 class="text-sm font-bold text-slate-800">(c) Derive the PDF $f_X(x)$ from your CDF.</h5>
            <button onclick="toggleSol('sol-1c')" class="mt-2 text-xs text-blue-600 hover:underline font-semibold">▶ Toggle Solution</button>
            <div id="sol-1c" class="hidden mt-2 p-3 bg-blue-50/60 rounded-lg text-sm space-y-1 border border-blue-100">
              <p>Differentiating $F_X(x)$ with respect to $x$ for $x > 0$:</p>
              <p>$$f_X(x) = \frac{d}{dx}\left[1 - \frac{1}{2}e^{-4x} - \frac{1}{2}e^{-2x}\right] = -\frac{1}{2}(-4e^{-4x}) - \frac{1}{2}(-2e^{-2x}) = 2e^{-4x} + e^{-2x}$$</p>
              <p>Thus:</p>
              <p>$$f_X(x) = \begin{cases} 2e^{-4x} + e^{-2x}, & x \ge 0 \\ 0, & x < 0 \end{cases}$$</p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <!-- (d) -->
          <div class="border-t pt-3">
            <h5 class="text-sm font-bold text-slate-800">(d) Calculate $F_X(0)$ and $F_X(1)$. Write down an equation that the median $m$ of $X$ must satisfy.</h5>
            <button onclick="toggleSol('sol-1d')" class="mt-2 text-xs text-blue-600 hover:underline font-semibold">▶ Toggle Solution</button>
            <div id="sol-1d" class="hidden mt-2 p-3 bg-blue-50/60 rounded-lg text-sm space-y-1 border border-blue-100">
              <p>• $F_X(0) = 1 - \frac{1}{2}e^{0} - \frac{1}{2}e^{0} = 1 - 0.5 - 0.5 = 0$.</p>
              <p>• $F_X(1) = 1 - \frac{1}{2}e^{-4} - \frac{1}{2}e^{-2} \approx 1 - 0.00916 - 0.06767 = 0.9232$.</p>
              <p>• The median $m$ satisfies $F_X(m) = 0.5$:</p>
              <p>$$1 - \frac{1}{2}e^{-4m} - \frac{1}{2}e^{-2m} = 0.5 \iff e^{-4m} + e^{-2m} = 1$$</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Question 2 -->
      <div class="border border-slate-200 rounded-xl overflow-hidden">
        <div class="bg-slate-100 p-4 border-b border-slate-200">
          <div class="flex justify-between items-center">
            <span class="font-bold text-blue-700">Question 2 [50 Points]</span>
            <span class="text-xs bg-white text-slate-700 px-2.5 py-1 rounded-md border font-medium">Symmetric Triangular Distribution</span>
          </div>
          <p class="text-sm mt-2 text-slate-800">
            Consider $g(x) = 2 - |x - \alpha|$ for $\alpha - 2 \le x \le \alpha + 2$ and $0$ otherwise.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="p-4 space-y-4">
          <!-- (a) -->
          <div>
            <h5 class="text-sm font-bold text-slate-800">(a) State the two properties of a valid PDF. Check whether $g(x)$ satisfies them.</h5>
            <button onclick="toggleSol('sol-2a')" class="mt-2 text-xs text-blue-600 hover:underline font-semibold">▶ Toggle Solution</button>
            <div id="sol-2a" class="hidden mt-2 p-3 bg-blue-50/60 rounded-lg text-sm space-y-1 border border-blue-100">
              <p><strong>Two properties:</strong> (1) $g(x) \ge 0$ for all $x$, and (2) $\int_{-\infty}^\infty g(x) dx = 1$.</p>
              <p><strong>Checking:</strong></p>
              <p>1. On $[\alpha-2, \alpha+2]$, $|x - \alpha| \le 2 \implies 2 - |x - \alpha| \ge 0$. Non-negativity holds.</p>
              <p>2. Integrate by substitution $u = x - \alpha$ ($du = dx$):</p>
              <p>$$\int_{\alpha-2}^{\alpha+2} (2 - |x - \alpha|)dx = \int_{-2}^2 (2 - |u|)du = 2\int_0^2 (2 - u)du = 2\left[2(2) - \frac{2^2}{2}\right] = 4 \ne 1$$</p>
              <p>(Geometrically, triangle base $= 4$, height $= 2$, Area $= \frac{1}{2}(4)(2) = 4$).</p>
              <p class="text-red-600 font-semibold">Thus, $g(x)$ is NOT a valid PDF because its total area is $4 \ne 1$.</p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <!-- (b) -->
          <div class="border-t pt-3">
            <h5 class="text-sm font-bold text-slate-800">(b) Find $c$ such that $f_X(x) = c(2 - |x - \alpha|)$ on $[\alpha-2, \alpha+2]$ is a valid PDF.</h5>
            <button onclick="toggleSol('sol-2b')" class="mt-2 text-xs text-blue-600 hover:underline font-semibold">▶ Toggle Solution</button>
            <div id="sol-2b" class="hidden mt-2 p-3 bg-blue-50/60 rounded-lg text-sm space-y-1 border border-blue-100">
              <p>$$\int_{-\infty}^\infty f_X(x) dx = c \int_{\alpha-2}^{\alpha+2} (2 - |x - \alpha|) dx = c \cdot 4 = 1 \implies c = \frac{1}{4}$$</p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <!-- (c) -->
          <div class="border-t pt-3">
            <h5 class="text-sm font-bold text-slate-800">(c) Calculate $E[X]$ and find the median $m$.</h5>
            <button onclick="toggleSol('sol-2c')" class="mt-2 text-xs text-blue-600 hover:underline font-semibold">▶ Toggle Solution</button>
            <div id="sol-2c" class="hidden mt-2 p-3 bg-blue-50/60 rounded-lg text-sm space-y-1 border border-blue-100">
              <p>The function $f_X(x)$ is symmetric about $x = \alpha$ because:</p>
              <p>$$f_X(\alpha + u) = \frac{1}{4}(2 - |u|) = f_X(\alpha - u)$$</p>
              <p>By symmetry of the distribution around $\alpha$:</p>
              <p>• $E[X] = \alpha$</p>
              <p>• Median $m = \alpha$ (since $\int_{-\infty}^\alpha f_X(x)dx = \frac{1}{2}(2)(1/2) = 0.5$).</p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <!-- (d) -->
          <div class="border-t pt-3">
            <h5 class="text-sm font-bold text-slate-800">(d) Is the distribution symmetric? Identify center. How does changing $\alpha$ affect location & shape?</h5>
            <button onclick="toggleSol('sol-2d')" class="mt-2 text-xs text-blue-600 hover:underline font-semibold">▶ Toggle Solution</button>
            <div id="sol-2d" class="hidden mt-2 p-3 bg-blue-50/60 rounded-lg text-sm space-y-1 border border-blue-100">
              <p>• <strong>Yes</strong>, it is symmetric around the center <strong>$x = \alpha$</strong>.</p>
              <p>• $\alpha$ is a pure <strong>location parameter</strong>. Changing $\alpha$ shifts the entire distribution along the x-axis horizontally (shifts center, mean, median) without changing the spread, height, or shape of the triangle at all.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Question 3 -->
      <div class="border border-slate-200 rounded-xl overflow-hidden">
        <div class="bg-slate-100 p-4 border-b border-slate-200">
