            <span class="font-bold text-blue-700">Question 3 [50 Points]</span>
            <span class="text-xs bg-white text-slate-700 px-2.5 py-1 rounded-md border font-medium">Normal Distribution Linear Transformations</span>
          </div>
          <p class="text-sm mt-2 text-slate-800">
            Let $X \sim N(4, 4)$ (mean $\mu=4$, variance $\sigma^2=4 \implies \sigma=2$), and let $Y = 2X + 1$.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="p-4 space-y-4">
          <!-- (a) -->
          <div>
            <h5 class="text-sm font-bold text-slate-800">(a) Explain why $Y$ is normally distributed. Find its mean, variance, and distribution.</h5>
            <button onclick="toggleSol('sol-3a')" class="mt-2 text-xs text-blue-600 hover:underline font-semibold">▶ Toggle Solution</button>
            <div id="sol-3a" class="hidden mt-2 p-3 bg-blue-50/60 rounded-lg text-sm space-y-1 border border-blue-100">
              <p>Any linear transformation $aX + b$ of a normal random variable remains normally distributed.</p>
              <p>• $E[Y] = E[2X + 1] = 2E[X] + 1 = 2(4) + 1 = 9$</p>
              <p>• $\text{Var}(Y) = \text{Var}(2X + 1) = 2^2 \text{Var}(X) = 4(4) = 16$</p>
              <p>• Distribution: <strong>$Y \sim N(9, 16)$</strong> (standard deviation $\sigma_Y = \sqrt{16} = 4$).</p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <!-- (b) -->
          <div class="border-t pt-3">
            <h5 class="text-sm font-bold text-slate-800">(b) Suppose $Z = dY - c$, with $d > 0$. Determine $d$ and $c$ such that $Z \sim N(0, 1)$.</h5>
            <button onclick="toggleSol('sol-3b')" class="mt-2 text-xs text-blue-600 hover:underline font-semibold">▶ Toggle Solution</button>
            <div id="sol-3b" class="hidden mt-2 p-3 bg-blue-50/60 rounded-lg text-sm space-y-1 border border-blue-100">
              <p>Standardizing $Y \sim N(9, 16)$ gives:</p>
              <p>$$Z = \frac{Y - \mu_Y}{\sigma_Y} = \frac{Y - 9}{4} = \frac{1}{4}Y - \frac{9}{4}$$</p>
              <p>Matching with $Z = dY - c$:</p>
              <p>$$d = \frac{1}{4} = 0.25, \quad c = \frac{9}{4} = 2.25$$</p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <!-- (c) -->
          <div class="border-t pt-3">
            <h5 class="text-sm font-bold text-slate-800">(c) Express $P(Y \le y)$ in terms of $\Phi$. Then calculate $P(Y \le 9)$.</h5>
            <button onclick="toggleSol('sol-3c')" class="mt-2 text-xs text-blue-600 hover:underline font-semibold">▶ Toggle Solution</button>
            <div id="sol-3c" class="hidden mt-2 p-3 bg-blue-50/60 rounded-lg text-sm space-y-1 border border-blue-100">
              <p>$$P(Y \le y) = P\left(\frac{Y - 9}{4} \le \frac{y - 9}{4}\right) = \Phi\left(\frac{y - 9}{4}\right)$$</p>
              <p>For $y = 9$:</p>
              <p>$$P(Y \le 9) = \Phi\left(\frac{9 - 9}{4}\right) = \Phi(0) = 0.5$$</p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <!-- (d) -->
          <div class="border-t pt-3">
            <h5 class="text-sm font-bold text-slate-800">(d) Express $q_Y(0.95)$ in terms of mean and SD of $Y$, using $z_{0.95} \approx 1.645$. Calculate it.</h5>
            <button onclick="toggleSol('sol-3d')" class="mt-2 text-xs text-blue-600 hover:underline font-semibold">▶ Toggle Solution</button>
            <div id="sol-3d" class="hidden mt-2 p-3 bg-blue-50/60 rounded-lg text-sm space-y-1 border border-blue-100">
              <p>The quantile equation is:</p>
              <p>$$q_Y(0.95) = \mu_Y + z_{0.95}\sigma_Y$$</p>
              <p>Substituting $\mu_Y = 9$ and $\sigma_Y = 4$:</p>
              <p>$$q_Y(0.95) = 9 + 1.645(4) = 9 + 6.58 = 15.58$$</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Question 4 -->
      <div class="border border-slate-200 rounded-xl overflow-hidden">
        <div class="bg-slate-100 p-4 border-b border-slate-200">
          <div class="flex justify-between items-center">
            <span class="font-bold text-blue-700">Question 4 [50 Points]</span>
            <span class="text-xs bg-white text-slate-700 px-2.5 py-1 rounded-md border font-medium">Heavy-Tailed Distribution & Moments</span>
          </div>
          <p class="text-sm mt-2 text-slate-800">
            Consider $f_X(x) = \frac{2}{(1+x)^3}$ for $x \ge 0$, and $0$ for $x < 0$.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="p-4 space-y-4">
          <!-- (a) -->
          <div>
            <h5 class="text-sm font-bold text-slate-800">(a) Does $E[X]$ exist as a finite number? If so, calculate it.</h5>
            <button onclick="toggleSol('sol-4a')" class="mt-2 text-xs text-blue-600 hover:underline font-semibold">▶ Toggle Solution</button>
            <div id="sol-4a" class="hidden mt-2 p-3 bg-blue-50/60 rounded-lg text-sm space-y-1 border border-blue-100">
              <p>$$E[X] = \int_0^\infty x \frac{2}{(1+x)^3} dx$$</p>
              <p>Let $u = 1 + x \implies x = u - 1$, $dx = du$ with bounds from $1$ to $\infty$:</p>
              <p>$$2 \int_1^\infty \frac{u - 1}{u^3} du = 2 \int_1^\infty \left(u^{-2} - u^{-3}\right) du = 2\left[ -u^{-1} + \frac{1}{2}u^{-2} \right]_1^\infty = 2\left[0 - \left(-1 + \frac{1}{2}\right)\right] = 2(0.5) = 1$$</p>
              <p><strong>Yes</strong>, $E[X]$ is finite and equals <strong>$1$</strong>.</p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <!-- (b) -->
          <div class="border-t pt-3">
            <h5 class="text-sm font-bold text-slate-800">(b) Does $E[X^2]$ exist as a finite number? If so, calculate it. If not, determine whether infinite or undefined.</h5>
            <button onclick="toggleSol('sol-4b')" class="mt-2 text-xs text-blue-600 hover:underline font-semibold">▶ Toggle Solution</button>
            <div id="sol-4b" class="hidden mt-2 p-3 bg-blue-50/60 rounded-lg text-sm space-y-1 border border-blue-100">
              <p>$$E[X^2] = \int_0^\infty x^2 \frac{2}{(1+x)^3} dx$$</p>
              <p>As $x \to \infty$, the integrand behaves like $\frac{2x^2}{x^3} = \frac{2}{x}$.</p>
              <p>Since $\int_1^\infty \frac{1}{x} dx$ diverges logarithmically ($\ln x \to \infty$), the integral diverges.</p>
              <p>Since the integrand is strictly non-negative, $E[X^2] = +\infty$. <strong>It is infinite (does not exist as a finite number).</strong></p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <!-- (c) -->
          <div class="border-t pt-3">
            <h5 class="text-sm font-bold text-slate-800">(c) Write the integral for $E[|X|^p]$ and check if finite for $p = 1/2$ and $p = 3$.</h5>
            <button onclick="toggleSol('sol-4c')" class="mt-2 text-xs text-blue-600 hover:underline font-semibold">▶ Toggle Solution</button>
            <div id="sol-4c" class="hidden mt-2 p-3 bg-blue-50/60 rounded-lg text-sm space-y-1 border border-blue-100">
              <p>Because $X \ge 0$, $|X| = X$. Thus:</p>
              <p>$$E[|X|^p] = \int_0^\infty \frac{2x^p}{(1+x)^3} dx$$</p>
              <p>For large $x$, the tail integrand behaves as $\frac{2 x^p}{x^3} = 2 x^{p-3} = \frac{2}{x^{3-p}}$.</p>
              <p>By the $p$-series test, $\int_1^\infty \frac{1}{x^k} dx$ converges if and only if $k > 1$. Here $k = 3 - p$.</p>
              <p>• For $p = 1/2$: $3 - p = 2.5 > 1 \implies$ <strong>Finite</strong>.</p>
              <p>• For $p = 3$: $3 - p = 0 \le 1 \implies$ <strong>Infinite</strong> ($+\infty$).</p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <!-- (d) -->
          <div class="border-t pt-3">
            <h5 class="text-sm font-bold text-slate-800">(d) What is the general rule on $p$ for $E[|X|^p]$ to be finite?</h5>
            <button onclick="toggleSol('sol-4d')" class="mt-2 text-xs text-blue-600 hover:underline font-semibold">▶ Toggle Solution</button>
            <div id="sol-4d" class="hidden mt-2 p-3 bg-blue-50/60 rounded-lg text-sm space-y-1 border border-blue-100">
              <p>For large $x$, convergence of $\int_c^\infty x^{p-3} dx$ requires the exponent $p - 3 < -1$, which means:</p>
              <p>$$3 - p > 1 \implies p < 2$$</p>
              <p>Near $x=0$, $x^p$ is integrable for any positive real $p > 0$. Hence $E[|X|^p]$ is finite if and only if <strong>$0 < p < 2$</strong>.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Question 5 (Bonus) -->
      <div class="border border-emerald-300 bg-emerald-50/30 rounded-xl overflow-hidden">
        <div class="bg-emerald-100/70 p-4 border-b border-emerald-200">
          <div class="flex justify-between items-center">
            <span class="font-bold text-emerald-800">Question 5 [10 Bonus Points]</span>
            <span class="text-xs bg-emerald-200 text-emerald-900 px-2.5 py-1 rounded-md font-semibold">Gamma Distribution Special Case</span>
          </div>
          <p class="text-sm mt-2 text-slate-800">
            Consider $f_X(x) = c x e^{-x}$ for $x \ge 0$, and $0$ for $x < 0$ ($c > 0$).
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="p-4 space-y-4">
          <!-- (a) -->
          <div>
            <h5 class="text-sm font-bold text-slate-800">(a) [3 pts] Find $c$ that makes $f_X(x)$ a valid PDF. Write it in terms of a gamma function.</h5>
            <button onclick="toggleSol('sol-5a')" class="mt-2 text-xs text-emerald-700 hover:underline font-semibold">▶ Toggle Solution</button>
            <div id="sol-5a" class="hidden mt-2 p-3 bg-white rounded-lg text-sm space-y-1 border border-emerald-200">
              <p>Recall $\Gamma(\alpha) = \int_0^\infty x^{\alpha-1} e^{-x} dx$. For $\alpha = 2$:</p>
              <p>$$\int_0^\infty x e^{-x} dx = \int_0^\infty x^{2-1} e^{-x} dx = \Gamma(2) = (2-1)! = 1$$</p>
              <p>Thus $c \int_0^\infty x e^{-x} dx = c \Gamma(2) = c(1) = 1 \implies c = \frac{1}{\Gamma(2)} = 1$.</p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <!-- (b) -->
          <div class="border-t border-emerald-200 pt-3">
            <h5 class="text-sm font-bold text-slate-800">(b) [3 pts] Calculate $P(0 \le X \le 1)$.</h5>
            <button onclick="toggleSol('sol-5b')" class="mt-2 text-xs text-emerald-700 hover:underline font-semibold">▶ Toggle Solution</button>
            <div id="sol-5b" class="hidden mt-2 p-3 bg-white rounded-lg text-sm space-y-1 border border-emerald-200">
              <p>Using integration by parts ($\int x e^{-x} dx = -x e^{-x} - e^{-x}$):</p>
              <p>$$P(0 \le X \le 1) = \int_0^1 x e^{-x} dx = \left[ -(x + 1)e^{-x} \right]_0^1 = -2e^{-1} - (-1e^0) = 1 - 2e^{-1} \approx 0.2642$$</p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <!-- (c) -->
          <div class="border-t border-emerald-200 pt-3">
            <h5 class="text-sm font-bold text-slate-800">(c) [2 pts] Calculate $E[e^{-2X}]$.</h5>
            <button onclick="toggleSol('sol-5c')" class="mt-2 text-xs text-emerald-700 hover:underline font-semibold">▶ Toggle Solution</button>
            <div id="sol-5c" class="hidden mt-2 p-3 bg-white rounded-lg text-sm space-y-1 border border-emerald-200">
              <p>$$E[e^{-2X}] = \int_0^\infty e^{-2x} (x e^{-x}) dx = \int_0^\infty x e^{-3x} dx$$</p>
              <p>Substitute $u = 3x \implies x = \frac{u}{3}, dx = \frac{du}{3}$:</p>
              <p>$$E[e^{-2X}] = \int_0^\infty \frac{u}{3} e^{-u} \frac{du}{3} = \frac{1}{9}\int_0^\infty u e^{-u} du = \frac{\Gamma(2)}{9} = \frac{1}{9}$$</p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <!-- (d) -->
          <div class="border-t border-emerald-200 pt-3">
            <h5 class="text-sm font-bold text-slate-800">(d) [2 pts] Is the distribution symmetric about its mean? Briefly explain.</h5>
            <button onclick="toggleSol('sol-5d')" class="mt-2 text-xs text-emerald-700 hover:underline font-semibold">▶ Toggle Solution</button>
            <div id="sol-5d" class="hidden mt-2 p-3 bg-white rounded-lg text-sm space-y-1 border border-emerald-200">
              <p><strong>No.</strong> It is right-skewed (positively skewed). Its support is bounded below at $0$ but unbounded above ($[0, \infty)$), with an exponential right tail that stretches to infinity.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Section 4: Interactive Study & Calculation Lab -->
    <section id="interactive-lab" class="bg-white rounded-2xl shadow-sm border border-slate-200 p-6 space-y-6">
      <div>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900">4. Interactive Calculation & Concept Verifier</h3>
        <p class="text-xs text-slate-500">Test parameters on the fly to build intuition for your exam.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
        
        <!-- Widget 1: Normal Calculator -->
        <div class="border p-4 rounded-xl bg-slate-50 space-y-3">
          <h4 class="font-bold text-sm text-slate-800">Normal Transformation Calculator</h4>
          <p class="text-xs text-slate-600">If $X \sim N(\mu, \sigma^2)$ and $Y = aX + b$, compute $E[Y]$, $\text{Var}(Y)$, and $\text{SD}(Y)$:</p>
          <div class="grid grid-cols-2 gap-2 text-xs">
            <div>
              <label class="block text-slate-600">Mean $\mu$</label>
              <input id="norm-mu" type="number" value="4" class="w-full p-1.5 border rounded" />
            </div>
            <div>
              <label class="block text-slate-600">Variance $\sigma^2$</label>
              <input id="norm-var" type="number" value="4" class="w-full p-1.5 border rounded" />
            </div>
            <div>
              <label class="block text-slate-600">Multiplier $a$</label>
              <input id="norm-a" type="number" value="2" class="w-full p-1.5 border rounded" />
            </div>
            <div>
              <label class="block text-slate-600">Shift $b$</label>
              <input id="norm-b" type="number" value="1" class="w-full p-1.5 border rounded" />
            </div>
          </div>
          <button onclick="calcNormal()" class="w-full bg-blue-600 text-white font-semibold py-1.5 rounded-lg text-xs hover:bg-blue-700">Calculate $Y$ Stats</button>
          <div id="norm-result" class="p-2 bg-white rounded border text-xs text-slate-800 font-mono">
            $E[Y] = 9$, $\text{Var}(Y) = 16$, $\text{SD}(Y) = 4$
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Widget 2: Exponential Mixture CDF -->
        <div class="border p-4 rounded-xl bg-slate-50 space-y-3">
          <h4 class="font-bold text-sm text-slate-800">Question 1 Exp Mixture CDF Checker</h4>
          <p class="text-xs text-slate-600">Evaluate $F_X(x) = 1 - 0.5e^{-4x} - 0.5e^{-2x}$ at any value $x$:</p>
          <div class="text-xs">
            <label class="block text-slate-600">Evaluate at $x$:</label>
            <input id="mix-x" type="number" step="0.1" value="1" class="w-full p-1.5 border rounded mt-1" />
          </div>
          <button onclick="calcMixCDF()" class="w-full bg-blue-600 text-white font-semibold py-1.5 rounded-lg text-xs hover:bg-blue-700">Evaluate $F_X(x)$</button>
          <div id="mix-result" class="p-2 bg-white rounded border text-xs text-slate-800 font-mono">
            $F_X(1) \approx 0.9232$
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Section 5: Rapid Fire Self-Quiz -->
    <section class="bg-gradient-to-r from-blue-900 to-indigo-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-6 space-y-4">
      <h3 class="text-xl font-bold">⚡ Rapid-Fire Concept Check</h3>
      <p class="text-xs text-blue-200">Test these high-frequency exam concepts:</p>
      
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-4 text-xs">
        <div class="bg-white/10 p-3 rounded-lg border border-white/10">
          <p class="font-bold">Q1: For any continuous RV $X$, what is $P(X = 3)$?</p>
          <button onclick="revealQuiz('qz1')" class="mt-2 text-blue-300 underline font-semibold">Show Answer</button>
          <p id="qz1" class="hidden mt-1 text-amber-300 font-bold">Exactly 0! Continuous probabilities over singletons are always 0.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="bg-white/10 p-3 rounded-lg border border-white/10">
          <p class="font-bold">Q2: If $\text{Var}(X) = 5$, what is $\text{Var}(-3X + 7)$?</p>
          <button onclick="revealQuiz('qz2')" class="mt-2 text-blue-300 underline font-semibold">Show Answer</button>
          <p id="qz2" class="hidden mt-1 text-amber-300 font-bold">$(-3)^2 \cdot \text{Var}(X) = 9 \times 5 = 45$.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="bg-white/10 p-3 rounded-lg border border-white/10">
          <p class="font-bold">Q3: Why does a standard Cauchy distribution have no mean?</p>
          <button onclick="revealQuiz('qz3')" class="mt-2 text-blue-300 underline font-semibold">Show Answer</button>
          <p id="qz3" class="hidden mt-1 text-amber-300 font-bold">$E[|X|] = \infty$. The split integral gives $\infty - \infty$, which is undefined.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="bg-white/10 p-3 rounded-lg border border-white/10">
          <p class="font-bold">Q4: If $X \sim \text{Exp}(4)$, what is $E[X]$?</p>
          <button onclick="revealQuiz('qz4')" class="mt-2 text-blue-300 underline font-semibold">Show Answer</button>
          <p id="qz4" class="hidden mt-1 text-amber-300 font-bold">$1/\lambda = 1/4 = 0.25$.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

  </main>

